License: Apache License, Version 2.0

Oh My Keymint adapts the public reply contract in an independent Rust
implementation. Android's RSA provider generates independent ASK and AuthKey
pairs per caller UID and exact UTF-16 alias. The reference ATTK signs ASK
exports, and each ASK signs its AuthKey exports using RSASSA-PSS/SHA-256.
Keys and signed exports are process-local. The cpu_id and device identifier
are derived from the unit serial, with per-process fallback identifiers.
No upstream C++ code or prebuilt binaries are bundled. Software-generated
mock replies are not genuine TEE attestation or payment credentials.

The Apache License 2.0 is included in AOSP.Apache-license-2.0.txt.
